HFD provider (src/israel_shipping_sdk/providers/hfd.py)
---------------------------------------------------------

The endpoint URLs, HTTP methods, authentication scheme, JSON field names,
and error-response shapes implemented in `providers/hfd.py` were determined
by inspecting the source code of:

    Plugin:   hfd-epost-integration
    Version:  2.21
    License:  GPLv2 or later
    Author:   HFD (per the plugin's own Author URI, https://www.hfd.co.il)
    Source:   https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/hfd-epost-integration.zip
              (official WordPress.org plugin repository)

Files consulted: class/Helper/Hfd/Api.php, class/Helper/Spot.php,
class/Admin.php, class/Setting.php, class/App.php.

What was extracted and what was not
------------------------------------

What was extracted is limited to interoperability facts: endpoint URLs,
HTTP verbs, JSON field names, status/error response shapes, and the
delivery-method-to-field-value mapping table HFD's own plugin uses. These
are functional facts about how to speak to HFD's API, not creative
expression.

No PHP source code, algorithm structure, comments, or variable-naming
choices from the plugin were copied, translated, or adapted into this
project. `providers/hfd.py` is written from scratch in idiomatic async
Python (pydantic models, httpx, a Strategy-pattern provider interface)
against the documented wire shapes — a different language, a different
architecture, and independent code, produced by reading the plugin only to
learn *what HFD's server expects on the wire*, not *how the plugin's PHP is
written*.

On license compatibility
--------------------------

This project's position is that documenting and reimplementing a wire
protocol for interoperability purposes — without copying source code — is
the same category of activity third-party API clients across the industry
are routinely built on, and does not carry the GPLv2 plugin's license
obligations forward into this independently-written, MIT-licensed
implementation. This is our stated rationale, not a legal opinion; a
maintainer taking this project further (in particular, toward wider
redistribution or commercial use) should have this reviewed by counsel
before relying on it, since the authors of this NOTICE are not lawyers.

Full spec, including exact endpoint tables and field mappings with their
provenance, is documented in the project's technical specification
(Section A.2).

Gov.il address data (src/israel_shipping_sdk/data/cities.json)
------------------------------------------------------------------

The bundled settlements fallback list was fetched from data.gov.il's public
CKAN API (dataset "citiesandsettelments", resource_id
8f714b6f-c35c-4b40-a0e7-547b675eee0e), which is published as Israeli
government open data. 1,310 records fetched and verified live.
